  "body": "Part of #2607 (slice S5 of 6).\n\nThe order of the maintainer (2026-11-18): \"GPU shader issues get priority\".\n\n## What\nReplace the dense GPU lattice with a sparse brick pool and a page table (Hoetzlein, GVDB, HPG 2016; Crassin et al., GigaVoxels, I3D 2009).\n\n- The dense lattice limits the display cell. Example: a 200 x 150 x 60 mm block at 0.25 mm is 460 MB for one f32 layer. This does not fit the 128 MiB default `maxStorageBufferBindingSize`.\n- The CPU makes the brick work list (S1, #2626). The GPU allocates and fills the bricks.\n- The trace shader reads through the page table.\n- The display cell follows the pixel size. `DEFAULT_TEXELS` in `crates/app/src/stock_view.rs` (line 39) is then for the CPU path only.\n\n## Tests\n- Parity: the sparse pool against the dense lattice on the same program, bit equal in the touched cells.\n- Measure on the large fixtures in release, against the frame target (#2238, under 10 ms for each frame). Write the readings in the PR.\n- Out of memory: refuse by name, and the dense or CPU path runs.\n\nBlocked by #2629 (S3).\n\nDone means: the GPU playback uses a sparse pool, shows a finer cell than today within the memory limits, and the parity tests and measurements are in the PR.\n",
